[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a breaking change to a published contract, so I want a yes before touching it.

  [38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m emits [38;5;153muserId[39m in [38;5;153mGET /users[39m. Per [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m, that response's field names are part of the contract,
  with three named consumers — the web app, iOS 3.2+, and the nightly partner export — and the README states contract
  changes go through a versioned endpoint. Renaming the field in place breaks all three at once: the iOS clients already
  shipped can't be updated in lockstep, and the partner export fails silently on the next nightly run.

  The rename itself is one line. The question is whether it lands as a break or behind a version.

